                <pb facs="1119" n="961" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg961"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Hitt to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-12-01"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">December 1,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Referring to department’s telegram of November 5, Mr. Hitt states that the
                    foreign office informs him that this Government will accept so-called white
                    certificates and withdraws requirement for certificate attesting microscopic
                    inspection of pork products, and that this decision has been telegraphed to
                    Italian ambassador at Washington with instructions to advise all Italian
                    consular officers in the United States accordingly.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
